  "notes": "Pennock's barn, dressed by trade (round 8, 8J): two straw-floored stalls either side of a planked aisle, the goats' troughs and buckets against the partitions, bales stacked in the west stall and thrown down under the loft, tack and long tools on the north boards between three storm lanterns, grain sacks, a water cask, the churns waiting for the cart and a stack of planks in the aisle, last year's scarecrow by the door. The goat bleats when anyone enters; the wolf's pelt hangs over the harness. The study key sits in a niche in the north boards (V1.5).",
